<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#"
     xml:base="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:dcterms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:owl2xml="http://www.w3.org/2006/12/owl2-xml#"
     xmlns:aquaticresources="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl#"
     xmlns:cpannotationschema="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/fsdas/aquaticresources.owl">
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <dcterms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent aquatic resources or stocks as composed of aquatic organisms from one or more species, and living in a water area.</dcterms:description>
        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Aquaticresources Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>What species are present in this aquatic resource/stock? In what water area this aquatic resource/stock lives in?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>Relations between aquatic resources and either aquatic species or water areas can be represented. In order to infer what species typically live in what water areas however, an application needs to add a SWRL rule, or a SPARQL query that unifies the hasSpecies and hasWaterArea relations.</cpannotationschema:hasConsequences>
        <cpannotationschema:hasIntent rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To represent aquatic resources or stocks as composed of aquatic organisms from one or more species, and living in a water area.</cpannotationschema:hasIntent>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>give me the Species for water area 24</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <cpannotationschema:scenarios>give me the Water areas for species Gadus morhua</cpannotationschema:scenarios>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x6; term declared x2;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Aquaticresources Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.1
changed hasWaterArea to canOccurIn</owl:versionInfo>
        <owl:versionInfo>Created by Aldo Gangemi</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


